## 2. Overall Goal and Research Questions

The overall goal of the thesis is to investigate and evaluate methods for reliable performance regression detection when numerical-analysis software is benchmarked across heterogeneous CI/CD environments.

In particular, the thesis will investigate whether benchmark results obtained on different or partially unknown hardware can be normalized or otherwise adjusted so that meaningful comparisons can be made against historical benchmark results without requiring the historical software versions to be rerun.

The thesis will address the following research questions:

1. **How does variation in the underlying execution environment affect the reliability and reproducibility of performance benchmarks for numerical algorithms in CI/CD environments?**

2. **To what extent can benchmark results for numerical applications be normalized across heterogeneous or partially unknown hardware environments?**

3. **What techniques or methods are most effective in normalizing infrastructure related performance variation?** 

The aim is not necessarily to eliminate all hardware-related variation, but to determine under which conditions reliable cross-environment comparisons are possible and what limitations remain.

