## 4. Scientific Foundation and Established Experience

The thesis will build upon existing research in software performance engineering, benchmarking, statistical performance analysis, reproducibility of experiments, and performance measurement in cloud and virtualized computing environments.

Particular attention will be given to previous work concerning performance regression detection and the statistical treatment of noisy benchmark measurements. Existing research concerning benchmarking in heterogeneous or virtualized environments will provide a foundation for understanding the effects of infrastructure variability.

The thesis will additionally draw on established practices in numerical analysis and scientific computing. NUMN21 provides a relevant application context through its focus on advanced numerical algorithms and the development, testing, and performance assessment of numerical software.

The scientific foundation will be established through a structured literature search using relevant academic databases and publications within software engineering, computer systems, numerical analysis, and scientific computing.

